window.docContents[104].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Kernel.Sys/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Kernel___Sys":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Kernel › Sys.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 6 headline theorems depend on it 141 of 185 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (13)def SYS_SET_TID_ADDRESSdef SYS_FUTEXdef FUTEX_WAKEdef FUTEX_PRIVATE_FLAGdef SYS_SCHED_GETAFFINITYdef SYS_GETPIDdef SYS_GETTIDdef SCHED_AFFINITY_MASKdef encodeSchedAffinityMaskdef execSetTidAddressdef execGetpiddef execSchedGetaffinitydef execFutex\n\nThread Identity, Futex Wake, and Affinity SyscallsLinux AArch64 syscall numbers and transition functions for set_tid_address (96), futex (98, FUTEX_WAKE / FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE), sched_getaffinity (123), getpid (172), and gettid (178), modeled after Linux kernel/fork.c, kernel/futex/, kernel/sched/syscalls.c, and kernel/sys.c in a single-process, single-thread, single-CPU environment.\n\n\n\ndef SYS_SET_TID_ADDRESSL28–29 ↗#Linux AArch64 set_tid_address syscall number (__NR_set_tid_address = 96, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:278, kernel/fork.c:1866).\n\ndef SYS_FUTEXL31–32 ↗#Linux AArch64 futex syscall number (__NR_futex = 98, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:270, kernel/futex/syscalls.c:191).\n\ndef FUTEX_WAKEL34–35 ↗#futex command FUTEX_WAKE (1, include/uapi/linux/futex.h:12).\n\ndef FUTEX_PRIVATE_FLAGL37–38 ↗#futex private-process flag FUTEX_PRIVATE_FLAG (128, include/uapi/linux/futex.h:26).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 40–41): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE\n\ndef SYS_SCHED_GETAFFINITYL43–44 ↗#Linux AArch64 sched_getaffinity syscall number (__NR_sched_getaffinity = 123, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:344, kernel/sched/syscalls.c:1395).\n\ndef SYS_GETPIDL46–47 ↗#Linux AArch64 getpid syscall number (__NR_getpid = 172, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:472, kernel/sys.c:966).\n\ndef SYS_GETTIDL49–50 ↗#Linux AArch64 gettid syscall number (__NR_gettid = 178, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:487, kernel/sys.c:979).\n\ndef SCHED_AFFINITY_MASKL52–54 ↗#8-byte kernel cpumask_t (CPU 0 online) written by sched_getaffinity under .singleCpu0.\n\ndef encodeSchedAffinityMaskL56–75 ↗#Serialize numWords 64-bit little-endian cpumask_t words masked to [0, nrCpuIds) bits, ensuring at least CPU 0 is active when words masks to all-zero (cpumask_and(&p->cpus_mask, cpu_active_mask) on a running thread always contains at least one active CPU).\n\ndef execSetTidAddressL77–82 ↗#set_tid_address(tidptr) (__NR_set_tid_address = 96, kernel/fork.c:1866): per Linux kernel/fork.c, records clear_child_tid ([INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: no-op in single-threaded execution without CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID) without dereferencing tidptr, and always succeeds returning the caller's thread ID (SIM_TID = 1).\n\ndef execGetpidL84–88 ↗#getpid() (__NR_getpid = 172, kernel/sys.c:966) and gettid() (__NR_gettid = 178, kernel/sys.c:979): return the calling process/thread ID (SIM_TID = 1) in the single-process, single-thread model ([INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]).\n\ndef execSchedGetaffinityL90–143 ↗#sched_getaffinity(pid, cpusetsize, mask) (__NR_sched_getaffinity = 123, kernel/sched/syscalls.c:1278,1307 SYSCALL_DEFINE3(sched_getaffinity, pid_t, pid, unsigned int, len, unsigned long __user *, user_mask_ptr) -> sched_getaffinity -> find_process_by_pid at kernel/sched/syscalls.c:215):* validates len (W1, 32-bit unsigned int) using exact 32-bit unsigned C arithmetic (len * BITS_PER_BYTE) < nr_cpu_ids ((len * 8#32) wraps modulo 2 ^ 32 when len has bits in [31:29], e.g. 0x20000000 or 0x80000000) and (len & 7) != 0 -> -EINVAL (kernel/sched/syscalls.c:1313-1316);* [INTENTIONAL_OVERAPPROX]: queries s.oracle.schedGetaffinity s.oracleIdx (SchedAffinityResult, defaulting to .singleCpu0) to over-approximate host nr_cpu_ids (1..8192), active cpumask_t bits, zalloc_cpumask_var -ENOMEM, and LSM security_task_getscheduler -EPERM;* if (pid : Int32) < 0 (pid.slt 0#32), returns -ESRCH (find_process_by_pid(pid) returns NULL in kernel/sched/syscalls.c:1284-1286);* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: if pid != 0 (calling thread) and pid != 1 (SIM_TID), fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled sched_getaffinity pid\";* writes retlen = min(len, cpumask_size()) bytes to mask (returning -EFAULT when mask + retlen > USER_VA_LIMIT or mask is unwritable at byte 0, and failing closed with .Exception on partial-fault copy_to_user) and returns retlen.\n\ndef execFutexL145–183 ↗#futex(uaddr, futex_op, val, ...) (__NR_futex = 98, SYSCALL_DEFINE6(futex) -> do_futex in kernel/futex/syscalls.c:108,191 -> futex_wake in kernel/futex/waitwake.c:178 -> get_futex_key in kernel/futex/core.c:514), modeled for FUTEX_WAKE (1) and FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE (129) in a single-process, single-thread environment:* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: op (W1, 32-bit int futex_op) outside FUTEX_WAKE (1) and FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE (129)—i.e. (op &&& 0xffffff7f#32) != FUTEX_WAKE, including FUTEX_WAIT, FUTEX_CLOCK_REALTIME (-ENOSYS), and FUTEX_ROBUST_UNLOCK—fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled futex op\";* for FUTEX_WAKE and FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE, futex_cmd_has_timeout is false (X3 ignored), futex_robust_unlock is a no-op (X4 ignored), X5 is ignored, and FLAGS_STRICT is unset so nr_wake (W2) is not constrained when zero waiters exist (waitwake.c:186,202);* if uaddr (X0) is not 4-byte-aligned (uaddr.toNat % 4 != 0), returns -EINVAL (kernel/futex/core.c:535, checked before access_ok);* if uaddr.toNat + 4 > USER_VA_LIMIT, returns EFAULT_RET (-EFAULT, access_ok in kernel/futex/core.c:539, include/asm-generic/access_ok.h:39);* for FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE ((op &&& FUTEX_PRIVATE_FLAG) != 0), get_futex_key keys on (current->mm, address) without faulting pages (kernel/futex/core.c:583-597) and futex_wake returns 0 (0 threads woken in single-threaded execution);* for shared FUTEX_WAKE (op == 1), get_futex_key probes get_user_pages_fast (kernel/futex/core.c:604-696): returns 0 when s.mem.canWrite uaddr 4, returns EFAULT_RET (-EFAULT) when [uaddr, uaddr + 4) is unmapped or PROT_NONE (!s.mem.allPerm (·.r) uaddr 4), and [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE] fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled shared futex on non-writable memory\" on read-only mappings (where Linux distinguishes anonymous ZERO_PAGE -EFAULT from file-backed 0).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Kernel/Sys.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Kernel.Sys/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Kernel___Sys"}});